  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe MCP `post` argument description now names `Tormach PathPilot Plasma`.\nThe MCP guide documents the Plasma Profile workflow on `Tormach 1300PL` with `PT-KERF-150`.\nA headless suite covers editing, undo, redo, generation, verification, posting and named refusals.\nThe bad-order fixture changes a saved path cache only inside the test.\nIt exercises the existing post gate through MCP.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe plasma machine, torch, operation and post had shipped.\nThe MCP post description omitted the plasma post name.\nThe MCP guide and workflow tests did not cover plasma.\nNo runtime safety guard needed a change.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll four pins pass:\n\n- `post_schema_advertises_the_builtin_plasma_post`\n- `plasma_profile_is_edited_undone_redone_generated_verified_and_posted_over_mcp`\n- `plasma_mcp_refuses_a_non_torch_nonzero_rpm_and_a_milling_post`\n- `plasma_mcp_reports_bad_cut_order_and_refuses_to_write_nc`\n\nThe schema pin failed on unchanged code and passed after the description fix.\nThe three behavior pins already passed on unchanged code.\nFor the mutation check, restoring the old `tools.rs` made the schema pin fail again.\nRestoring the fix made it pass again.\nNo new runtime guard was added.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed: 357 passed, 1 ignored, 38 seconds.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nThe gate used base `ae601e476c9fab62c13ef9d7845e77d744dff589`.\nAnother session moved the shared `upstream/main` ref afterward.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical plasma table or UI was exercised.\nThe 3D stock simulation does not run for plasma.\nThe tests check the reported 2D plasma verdict and its blocking failures.\nLatest upstream changes after base `ae601e476` were not integrated.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #1738 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIt changes `all()` in `tools.rs`; this PR changes `s_post()`.\nIts MCP guide changes concern WCS rows.\nPR #1817 touches the same guide, different section; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIt adds a Pocket rest-machining row; this PR appends a Plasma Profile section.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: MCP advertises the Tormach PathPilot Plasma post and documents its tested Plasma Profile workflow.\n\nFixes #1871\n",
